    "narrative": "For LawDog today, the offensive engine is centered on a favorable matchup against Ritchie, with three of our top performers\u2014**Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81), **Tyler Freeman** (72.12), and **Matt Chapman** (70.06)\u2014leading the charge. **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our highest-rated play, buoyed by a soft 5.41 xERA matchup against Aldegheri and a +8% boost from his #2 hole placement. Meanwhile, **Matt Chapman** and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) benefit significantly from the +19% SP skill advantage provided by the Ritchie start. We are also monitoring **Lawrence Butler** closely; while his 57.16 score is mid-tier, his +10% park factor and +13% platoon advantage make him a high-upside play if he can capitalize on the favorable conditions against Ashcraft.\n\nThe benching of **Taylor Ward** (45.02) was the most difficult decision of the morning. While his projected leadoff spot would usually be a primary driver for selection, the combination of a tough 3.60 xERA matchup against Kirby and a negative park factor pushed him below our active threshold. We are also tracking a notable risk with **Tyler Freeman**, who carries a 43% rain risk; should he be scratched, we will have to pivot quickly to ensure we don\u2019t lose plate appearances in a high-value spot. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining on the IL and **Yainer Diaz** out of today\u2019s lineup, our depth is being tested, but the projected outputs for **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) and **Bryson Stott** (66.80) provide the necessary stability to keep LawDog competitive across our 5x5 categories.",
